      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Astor Academy Playwrights Study Circle"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Are you interet interested in learning about theatre and famous theatre playwrights?  </p>\\n<p>Join Katherine Schellmer in the Playwrights Study Circle!  A brand new Astor Academy designed for adults.  Meeting on Friday evenings in our Gorham Room, this program will provide a fun, informative learning experience. Katherine has written professionally for theatre, TV, radio, and film.  She was also an educator at The National Theatre School of Canada for three years, running a sessional course entitled “Solo Show” in which she mentored and then directed students performing their own works. </p>\\n<p>She hopes to use her experience/knowledge to invigorate the theatre community in Queens County.</p>\\n<p>In this program, the group study a specific playwright, as well as the time period the play was written in; world events, cultural events, the forces that shaped the creation of the work, and the<br />\\nreaction to the work when it premiered.</p>\\n"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
